  {
    "path": "/private/rounds/1/manual_recap",
    "old_sha256": "a54bcb1d5b762089ba5a8e99415b105688d29b687ad77784632870aa045895a2",
    "value": "validate_batch is delivered and settled, including its index-and-message errors list; new work must reuse it, not reimplement it. This round adds group_submissions(batch): a non-list batch returns the validator's error object unchanged; otherwise the result is {\"ok\": true, \"groups\": {assignment: [records]}, \"errors\": [...]}, where groups keyed by the exact normalized assignment name hold the normalized records in their original arrival order, and errors is the validator's errors list carried over unchanged — reporting invalid entries this way is now also grouping's own contract, established by its request. Averages in the groups were suggested by the assistant and explicitly declined — grouping reports no averages. Standing rules continue: JSON in, JSON-safe object out, never raise; every attempt kept, resubmissions included, never merged; sorting or reordering remains prohibited, inside each group as well. Scoped change this round: the earlier two-decimal rounding instruction is retired; from now on any reported average is rounded to one decimal. That convention has no consumer yet and first applies to the summary feature."
  },
